.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/fast-deep-equal Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "fast-deep-equal"
.PP
The fastest deep equal with ES6 Map, Set and Typed arrays support\&.

.PP
\fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install fast\-deep\-equal
.fi
.PP
.SH "Features"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
ES5 compatible
.IP "\(bu" 2
works in node\&.js (8+) and browsers (IE9+)
.IP "\(bu" 2
checks equality of Date and RegExp objects by value\&.
.PP

.PP
ES6 equal (\fRrequire('fast-deep-equal/es6')\fP) also supports:
.IP "\(bu" 2
Maps
.IP "\(bu" 2
Sets
.IP "\(bu" 2
Typed arrays
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
var equal = require('fast\-deep\-equal');
console\&.log(equal({foo: 'bar'}, {foo: 'bar'})); // true
.fi
.PP

.PP
To support ES6 Maps, Sets and Typed arrays equality use:

.PP
.PP
.nf
var equal = require('fast\-deep\-equal/es6');
console\&.log(equal(Int16Array([1, 2]), Int16Array([1, 2]))); // true
.fi
.PP

.PP
To use with React (avoiding the traversal of React elements' _owner property that contains circular references and is not needed when comparing the elements - borrowed from \fRreact-fast-compare\fP):

.PP
.PP
.nf
var equal = require('fast\-deep\-equal/react');
var equal = require('fast\-deep\-equal/es6/react');
.fi
.PP
